cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository or its computational model, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Dynamic Risk Surface Modelling of Cytopenia Recovery and Infection Vulnerability During Bispecific Antibody Therapy in High-Risk Lymphoma"

type: software

authors:
  - given-names: "Prihantini"

repository-code: "https://github.com/TitinPrihantini4/bispecific-dynamic-risk-surface-model"

abstract: >-
  This repository contains the executable code, model inputs,
  model-generated outputs, figures, and manuscript for a
  literature-parameterized computational proof-of-concept of
  cytopenia recovery and infection vulnerability during
  bispecific-antibody therapy. The framework integrates a
  nonlinear dynamic reserve-stress-hazard model with scenario
  analysis, global and local sensitivity analysis, stochastic
  uncertainty propagation, latent-regime summaries, numerical
  robustness assessment, synthetic mechanism recovery, and
  structural exposure-schedule sensitivity. No patient-level
  clinical data were used for model fitting or validation, and
  the reported numerical outputs should not be interpreted as
  observed clinical incidences, validated risk estimates,
  treatment effects, or clinical decision thresholds.

keywords:
  - "bispecific antibody"
  - "cytopenia"
  - "dynamic risk surface"
  - "infection vulnerability"
  - "mathematical modelling"
  - "regime switching"
  - "ordinary differential equations"
  - "computational modelling"

license: "MIT"
